※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4921 LANG_ENTRY_NOT_A_PARAMETER

※ What is written between the brackets has to be one of the function's own
※ parameters.  A local of the body has no value at entry -- the body had not
※ run -- and a variable at the top level is not the call's to speak about.

let counter: u8 = 1u8

fn step(a: u8) → u8 post(⎕entry(counter) > 0u8):
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(step(1u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
